Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi,

I am currently trying to plot several clade names in a circular tree with something like this:

> head(cladesData)
clades  node     col
capensis   5497 #000000
hemprichii 11453 #FF7F00
lemniscatus  7407 #7FC97F
patagonicus 11563 #666666
gambianus  7666 #1F78B4
argenteus 11811 #BF5B17

 p <- ggtree(tree, layout="circular")
 for (i in 1:length(cladesData$clades)){
    p <- p + geom_hilight(node=cladesData[i, 'node'], fill = cladesData[i, 'col'], alpha = .3) +
    geom_cladelabel(node = cladesData[i,'node'], label = cladesData[i],
                    color = cladesData[i,'col'], offset = .8, align = TRUE)
}

Where I get something like this tree in attach. I would like to know if there is a way that the clades names in the left can be aligned around the tree similarly to the names in the right. If the plotting can be done in a way that the end of the words in the left is closer to the highlight while the words in the right are already good with the beginning of the word starting near the highlight. If not, is there a way that the clade names could be written in a circular format following the tree circularity?

Thanks for any help you can provide

